{
  "reference_answer": "Not really, and the main reason is the pace. I've stayed with friends in a big city a few times, and after about three days I felt permanently wired — the noise never fully stops, even at night. What gets me is that you can't just step outside and hear yourself think. I'd take a smaller town any day, as long as it's got a decent train link, because then I can dip into the city when I actually want it and come back to quiet. So it's less about avoiding cities and more about not living in the middle of one.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：以“城市节奏让人持续紧绷”为核心，用短住体验说明，再以“小城镇+便利交通”作为条件式选择；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "permanently wired",
      "meaning_zh": "一直处于紧绷、亢奋、放松不下来的状态",
      "why_useful": "比 very stressed 更具体，能自然描述环境对人的持续影响，适合城市、工作、考试等话题。",
      "example": "After a week of back-to-back meetings I felt permanently wired.",
      "usage_note": "口语中常跟 feel / felt 搭配，语气偏非正式。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "hear yourself think",
      "meaning_zh": "有安静的环境可以思考、静下心来",
      "why_useful": "高频地道表达，常用于抱怨噪音或强调需要安静空间，迁移到学习、居住、旅行场景都很自然。",
      "example": "The café was so crowded I couldn't hear myself think.",
      "usage_note": "多用于否定句 can't / couldn't。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "dip into",
      "meaning_zh": "偶尔体验一下、短暂参与",
      "why_useful": "比 go to 更有“按需短暂享受”的含义，适合表达有条件地接触某事物，如城市生活、文化活动。",
      "example": "I like to dip into the city for concerts but I wouldn't want to live there.",
      "usage_note": "后面常接地点或活动，强调短暂而非长期投入。"
    }
  ]
